## Tools and Interfaces

- [InfluxDB 3 Explorer](https://docs.influxdata.com/influxdb3/explorer/get-started/): User interface for connecting to InfluxDB 3, writing data, querying data, and exploring time series datasets where supported.
- [InfluxDB 3 MCP Server](https://docs.influxdata.com/influxdb3/enterprise/admin/mcp-server/): Use for connecting LLM agents to query or manage InfluxDB 3.
- [Processing Engine Plugins](https://www.influxdata.com/products/processing-engine-plugins/): Official plugins for anomaly detection, forecasting, transformation, monitoring, alerts, and ingestion workflows.
- [System Metrics plugin](https://www.influxdata.com/processing-engine-plugins/system-metrics/): Collect CPU, memory, disk, and network metrics from the InfluxDB 3 host.
- [Basic Transformation plugin](https://www.influxdata.com/processing-engine-plugins/basic-transformation/): Transform field and tag names, convert values, and standardize time series data in real time or on a schedule.
- [Downsampler plugin](https://www.influxdata.com/processing-engine-plugins/downsampler/): Roll raw data into lower-resolution summaries for retention, query performance, and cost control.
- [Chronos Forecasting plugin](https://www.influxdata.com/processing-engine-plugins/chronos-forecasting/): Use pre-trained Chronos models for zero-shot time series forecasting in InfluxDB 3.
- [MQTT Subscriber plugin](https://www.influxdata.com/processing-engine-plugins/mqtt-subscriber/): Subscribe to MQTT topics and ingest MQTT messages directly into InfluxDB 3.
- [InfluxDB 3 client libraries](https://docs.influxdata.com/influxdb3/cloud-serverless/reference/client-libraries/v3/): Language-specific client libraries for writing and querying InfluxDB 3.
